From cecb2931d0e371f21add80fc0bac7ee9e57fec83 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 17:28:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] generic-parallel: Kokkos and SYCL backends, GPU offloading
 with nvc++

Backends of the `generic-parallel` interface for behaviours:

- the integration at one point is a trivially copyable function object
  (`PointIntegrator`), selected according to the storage of the fields
  (`dispatch`), and used by the `stlpar`, `kokkos` and `sycl` backends;
- `kokkos` backend: `Kokkos::parallel_reduce` with a reduction functor, in
  the execution space given by the `execution_space` option; the stack size
  of GPU threads is computed from a probe kernel;
- `sycl` backend: `parallel_for` with atomic updates of the statistics of
  the batch, automatic transfers of the fields which are not accessible by
  the device (`data_transfer_policy` option, as for material properties);
- `stlpar` backend: offloading to NVIDIA GPUs with `nvc++ -stdpar=gpu`
  (`-gpu=mem:managed` in the `stlpar-parunseq-nvhpc-gpu` configuration);
- `device_stack_size` option of the `stlpar` and `sycl` backends, for
  behaviours and material properties: the stack size of the threads is set
  through the CUDA runtime loaded by the process
  (`MFront/GenericParallel/DeviceStackSize.hxx`), since `nvc++` and
  AdaptiveCpp give no access to it.

Tests and configurations:

- tests `kokkos`, `kokkos-host`, `sycl-default-acpp`,
  `sycl-default-acpp-omp` and `stlpar-parunseq-nvhpc-gpu`;
- `kokkos` configuration: compiler and flags extracted from the imported
  targets of Kokkos;
- the substitution of a compiler is also defined when the compiler is given
  by the user, and `HIP_PLATFORM` is cached.
